                                                "example_id": "d1b54887-4961-4c5a-9c4f-21341b4bccff",
                                                "sense_id": "39ade29e-d391-3b6e-a65b-3a730eb4cb9e",
                                                "text": "It is everywhere observed that a liberated slave is apt to make a merciless master, and that boys who have been cruelly fagged at school are cruel faggers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faa05f41-5743-3276-9039-9f2773105bdd",
                                        "entry_id": "16127286-42da-3f66-9f43-0b5b33c4f1dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work hard, especially on menial chores."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03d0e39c-ccf7-41b0-88b8-aff578f160a8",
                                                "sense_id": "faa05f41-5743-3276-9039-9f2773105bdd",
                                                "text": "This state of things should have been to me a paradise of peace, accustomed as I was to a life of ceaseless reprimand and thankless fagging; but, in fact, my racked nerves were now in such a state that no calm could soothe, and no pleasure excite them agreeably."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8a94ab4-c64d-4fa4-95bf-7a087c4f0a02",
                                                "sense_id": "faa05f41-5743-3276-9039-9f2773105bdd",
                                                "text": "I walked about the streets where the best shops for ladies were, I haunted the Bazaar like an unquiet spirit, I fagged through the Park again and again, long after I was quite knocked up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fag",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                        "entry_id": "6f539a5d-3ed7-32e8-bee5-91e64f1ba720",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A homosexual man, especially (usually derogatory) an effeminate or unusual one."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US",
                                            "endearing",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "usually",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "022eda24-ddc5-4e6d-ad4c-26c826d4fa22",
                                                "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                                "text": "1921 John Lind, The Female Impersonators (Historical Documentation of American Slang v. 1, A-G, edited by Jonathan E. Lighter (New York: Random House, 1994) page 716.\nAndrogynes known as “fairies,” “fags,” or “brownies.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8e16af3-df1d-497e-9c04-b8b15b7b3a62",
                                                "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                                "text": "In schizophrenics, however, the homosexual outlet is sooner or later ... ideas that strangers call them \"cs,\" \"fairy,\" \"woman,\" \"fag,\" \" fruit,\" etc.). ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4a5d8e1-d758-4dcc-87a1-bbb03969212c",
                                                "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                                "text": "When they pick out a set of clubs for him to rent, he is so indifferent and silent the freckled kid in charge stares at him as if he's a moron. The thought flits through his brain that Eccles is known as a fag and he has become the new pet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb5eb582-089f-4189-a6c6-476612c45ebb",
                                                "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                                "text": "A couple of days later, Trisha tells Madelyn there is a rumor going around that she's a fag."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2cc8b0b-cd1d-482a-8572-29eccb7ffe9d",
                                                "sense_id": "4d95777f-9094-3684-8e2a-dba6fc4e63a3",
                                                "text": "... what appeared to be overt appeals to anti-gay sentiment. When House Majority Whip Dick Armey referred to fellow Congressman Barney Frank as \"Barney Fag\" in 1995, he suffered a barage of negative publicity that prompted him to explain his choice of words as a slip of the tongue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03bd7541-81df-3dd1-aac0-1c1291012d22",
                                        "entry_id": "6f539a5d-3ed7-32e8-bee5-91e64f1ba720",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An annoying person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "915dc7f6-59a1-4683-b3bd-50c77f1200b2",
                                                "sense_id": "03bd7541-81df-3dd1-aac0-1c1291012d22",
                                                "text": "Why did you do that, you fag?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
